<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Schwarzburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Schwarzburg was a Thuringian noble family, counts from the 12th century, whose lands lay around Schwarzburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnstadt">Arnstadt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sondershausen">Sondershausen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a>. In 1349 Günther of Schwarzburg was elected German king against Charles IV, and on his withdrawal the family received pledged lands such as Gelnhausen. Its branches became the principalities of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt and Schwarzburg-Sondershausen, which lasted until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-schwarzburg.jpg" alt="House of Schwarzburg" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nomadic1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CoA_Schwarzburg_County.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
